## 4. Understanding 2D Arrays

Example:

```java
int[][] accounts = {
    {2, 8, 7},
    {7, 1, 3},
    {1, 9, 5}
};
```

Visual representation:

| Customer / Row | Bank 0 | Bank 1 | Bank 2 |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| Customer 0 | 2 | 8 | 7 |
| Customer 1 | 7 | 1 | 3 |
| Customer 2 | 1 | 9 | 5 |

### Important syntax

```java
accounts[i]
```
Accesses an entire row.

```java
accounts[i][j]
```
Accesses one particular element.

**Remember:**

- `i` = Row / Customer
- `j` = Column / Bank account

